[long_report.txt#2] (section: Retrieval System Design Notes)
The cleaning stage takes that raw text and makes it consistent across every source format. It normalizes Unicode so visually identical characters compare equal, repairs a handful of common encoding artifacts, and unifies line endings so downstream code never has to branch on whether a file came from Windows or Unix. Repeated running headers and footers, such as page counters, are detected and removed so they do not pollute every chunk with the same boilerplate line.

[long_report.txt#5] (section: Retrieval System Design Notes)
The second strategy respects the paragraph structure of the document, grouping whole paragraphs together up to a size limit, and only falling back to splitting a paragraph by sentence when a single paragraph is larger than that limit on its own.

